{"id":"e13c87067d559828","group":"58","path":"58/batch07/58-df-random-walk.md","title":"Random Walk","display":"df-random-walk — Random Walk","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-random-walk","aliases":["58-df-random-walk","Random Walk"],"display":"df-random-walk — Random Walk","depends_on":["[[58-df-iid]]","[[../batch09/58-df-group.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-random-walk"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-random-walk</span><span>Random Walk</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-random-walk — Random Walk"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"64b5bf078722d744\" href=\"?note=64b5bf078722d744\" title=\"58-df-iid\">58-df-iid</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"ed71f39f59370734\" href=\"?note=ed71f39f59370734\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-group.md\">../batch09/58-df-group.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\">\\((\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)\\)</span> (probability space)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(G,\\mathcal G,+)\">\\((G,\\mathcal G,+)\\)</span> (measurable abelian state group)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Group}_S(G,+)\">\\(\\mathrm{Group}_S(G,+)\\)</span> (group predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"ed71f39f59370734\" href=\"?note=ed71f39f59370734\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-group.md\">../batch09/58-df-group.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x_0\\in G\">\\(x_0\\in G\\)</span> (initial state)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\xi\\in(G^\\Omega)^\\omega\">\\(\\xi\\in(G^\\Omega)^\\omega\\)</span> (increment sequence)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S\\in(G^\\Omega)^\\omega\">\\(S\\in(G^\\Omega)^\\omega\\)</span> (process candidate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu\">\\(\\mu\\)</span> (common increment law)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{IID}_S(\\xi,\\omega,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,G,\\mathcal G)\">\\(\\mathrm{IID}_S(\\xi,\\omega,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,G,\\mathcal G)\\)</span> (i.i.d. predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"64b5bf078722d744\" href=\"?note=64b5bf078722d744\" title=\"58-df-iid\">58-df-iid</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{RandomWalk}_S(S,\\xi,x_0,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,G,\\mathcal G)\">\\(\\operatorname{RandomWalk}_S(S,\\xi,x_0,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,G,\\mathcal G)\\)</span> (random-walk predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}random\\text{-}walk} \\vdash \\operatorname{RandomWalk}_S(S,\\xi,x_0,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,G,\\mathcal G) \\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Group}_S(G,+)\\land\\forall x,y\\in G\\;(x+y=y+x)\\land x_0\\in G\\land S\\in(G^\\Omega)^\\omega\\land\\xi\\in(G^\\Omega)^\\omega\\land\\mathrm{IID}_S(\\xi,\\omega,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,G,\\mathcal G)\\land\\forall\\omega_0\\in\\Omega\\;\\bigl(S(0)(\\omega_0)=x_0\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(S(n+1)(\\omega_0)=S(n)(\\omega_0)+\\xi(n)(\\omega_0))\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}random\\text{-}walk} \\vdash \\operatorname{RandomWalk}_S(S,\\xi,x_0,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,G,\\mathcal G) \\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Group}_S(G,+)\\land\\forall x,y\\in G\\;(x+y=y+x)\\land x_0\\in G\\land S\\in(G^\\Omega)^\\omega\\land\\xi\\in(G^\\Omega)^\\omega\\land\\mathrm{IID}_S(\\xi,\\omega,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,G,\\mathcal G)\\land\\forall\\omega_0\\in\\Omega\\;\\bigl(S(0)(\\omega_0)=x_0\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(S(n+1)(\\omega_0)=S(n)(\\omega_0)+\\xi(n)(\\omega_0))\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Random walk: sum of i.i.d. increments</li>\n<li>Simple random walk on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb Z^d\">\\(\\mathbb Z^d\\)</span> has increments uniformly distributed on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\{\\pm e_1,\\ldots,\\pm e_d\\}\">\\(\\{\\pm e_1,\\ldots,\\pm e_d\\}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Moment identities require finite first/second moments; return asymptotics also require dimension-dependent constants and parity conditions, so neither belongs to the definition.</li>\n<li>Recurrence: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"d=1,2\">\\(d=1,2\\)</span> recurrent; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"d \\geq 3\">\\(d \\geq 3\\)</span> transient</li>\n<li>Donsker: scaled RW converges to Brownian motion</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Lawler and Limic, Random Walk: A Modern Introduction</li>\n<li>Spitzer, Principles of Random Walk</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-iid","status":"resolved","id":"64b5bf078722d744","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-iid]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch09/58-df-group.md","status":"resolved","id":"ed71f39f59370734","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-group.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch09/58-df-group.md","status":"resolved","id":"ed71f39f59370734","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Group}_S(G,+)$ (group predicate, see [[../batch09/58-df-group.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-iid","status":"resolved","id":"64b5bf078722d744","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{IID}_S(\\xi,\\omega,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,G,\\mathcal G)$ (i.i.d. predicate, see [[58-df-iid]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)","display":false},{"tex":"(G,\\mathcal G,+)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Group}_S(G,+)","display":false},{"tex":"x_0\\in G","display":false},{"tex":"\\xi\\in(G^\\Omega)^\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"S\\in(G^\\Omega)^\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\mu","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{IID}_S(\\xi,\\omega,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,G,\\mathcal G)","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{RandomWalk}_S(S,\\xi,x_0,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,G,\\mathcal G)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}random\\text{-}walk} \\vdash \\operatorname{RandomWalk}_S(S,\\xi,x_0,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,G,\\mathcal G) \\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Group}_S(G,+)\\land\\forall x,y\\in G\\;(x+y=y+x)\\land x_0\\in G\\land S\\in(G^\\Omega)^\\omega\\land\\xi\\in(G^\\Omega)^\\omega\\land\\mathrm{IID}_S(\\xi,\\omega,\\mu;\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P,G,\\mathcal G)\\land\\forall\\omega_0\\in\\Omega\\;\\bigl(S(0)(\\omega_0)=x_0\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;(S(n+1)(\\omega_0)=S(n)(\\omega_0)+\\xi(n)(\\omega_0))\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathbb Z^d","display":false},{"tex":"\\{\\pm e_1,\\ldots,\\pm e_d\\}","display":false},{"tex":"d=1,2","display":false},{"tex":"d \\geq 3","display":false}],"bytes":1959,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1035","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-random-walk.md|58-df-random-walk]]（batch07）"}],"outgoing":["64b5bf078722d744","ed71f39f59370734"]}